topics.detail:
AI Not Needed argues that AI has no good uses. AI undermines human knowledge and humanity. AI Trust argues that AI is good at fetching data. AI is used for supply chains.

@thatqueerharpy.bsky.social: “its either too good and its AI or its so bad its AI. You can't win. I'm sorry this happened to you. Keep being goated, King.”

AI Not Needed (93.8%) says AI is not beneficial. AI Trust (6.2%) says AI is trusted for data tasks.

AI Not Welcome argues that AI undercuts research quality. AI is unsuitable for creative tasks like publishing and fiction. AI Limitations argues that AI buildout has no particular reason. AI boosters claimed something was impossible due to expense. AI makes some tasks easier but not others.

@mgerrydoyle.bsky.social: “yeah, I would say of all the things in the world that ai is neither welcome nor helpful in, it's publishing and especially fiction I want a person responding to my words and helping me improve them, not an algorithm that has gobbled up decades of bestseller lists in "learning…”

AI Not Welcome (73.3%) says AI is neither welcome nor helpful. AI Limitations (26.7%) says AI has limitations.

