Business.detail:
Wealth Disparity argues that a few people have skimmed billions into offshore accounts. A single billion dollars is a staggering amount of money. Record Spending argues that computer prices are up a record 17%. US treasury borrows record $839 billion.

@wellborn.net: “Sergey Brin preemptively fled to Nevada to dodge $12 billion, then dropped $102 million rigging two decoy propositions designed to cancel out the wealth tax he's scared of. He named one of them fiscal responsibility.”

Wealth Disparity (77.4%) says Some individuals have excessive wealth. Record Spending (22.6%) says Companies are spending record amounts.

Culture.detail:
Podcast Endorsements argues that podcasts are thoroughly enjoyable. some podcasts are very good once you skip the bad parts. certain podcasters are excellent interviewers and storytellers. Podcasts Suck argues that Podcasts have significant drawbacks.

@andreapitzer.bsky.social: “The Friday roundup is here, with links to the podcast! I also wrote about the challenge of keeping up with the latest infuriating developments, and why sometimes it's a good idea to step away from the news and do something tangible to make a difference.”

Podcast Endorsements (72.2%) says Podcasts are enjoyable. Podcasts Suck (27.8%) says Podcasts have significant drawbacks.

Health.detail:
Animal Cruelty argues that forcing animals to fight is inhumane. Hunting animals is abusive. Using animals in police and war is abuse. Animal Welfare argues that Sanctuaries provide a safe home for animals. Animals are individuals deserving of love and care. Animal rescuers provide a better life for animals.

@gwendolyn-corvid.bsky.social: “Today's Fit: Going to dinner at animal kingdom.”

Animal Cruelty (83%) says Animals are treated cruelly. Animal Welfare (17%) says Animals deserve care and love.

